    "examples": [
      {
        "question_text": "Evaluate by writing the repeated factors.\n(a) $(-4)^2$\n(b) $(-2)^3$",
        "solution_text": "(a) $(-4)^2=(-4)\\times(-4)=16$.\nTwo negative factors give a positive product.\n(b) $(-2)^3=(-2)\\times(-2)\\times(-2)=4\\times(-2)=-8$.\nThe first two negative signs pair up, leaving one negative factor."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "State whether each value is positive or negative. Do not work out the value.\n(a) $(-11)^{16}$\n(b) $(-6)^{13}$\n(c) $9^7$",
        "solution_text": "(a) Positive: the negative base has an even index, so all the negative signs pair up.\n(b) Negative: the negative base has an odd index, leaving one negative sign after pairing.\n(c) Positive: all seven factors are positive."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "Evaluate each pair. Explain how the brackets affect the base.\n(a) $(-6)^2$ and $-6^2$\n(b) $(-2)^5$ and $-2^5$",
        "solution_text": "(a) $(-6)^2=(-6)\\times(-6)=36$.\n$-6^2=-(6\\times6)=-36$.\nThe bracketed base includes the negative sign. Without brackets, square $6$ first and then take its negative.\n(b) $(-2)^5=(-2)\\times(-2)\\times(-2)\\times(-2)\\times(-2)=-32$.\n$-2^5=-(2\\times2\\times2\\times2\\times2)=-32$.\nThe bases are different, but the answers agree here: five negative factors give a negative result, and the separate minus sign also gives a negative result."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "Use each given value to write down the answers.\n(a) Given $5^4=625$, find $(-5)^4$ and $-5^4$.\n(b) Given $6^3=216$, find $(-6)^3$.",
        "solution_text": "(a) $(-5)^4=625$: four negative signs pair up, so the value is positive and has the same size as $5^4$.\n$-5^4=-625$: the minus sign is outside the power.\n(b) $(-6)^3=-216$: three negative factors give a negative result with the same size as $6^3$."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "(a) Given $(-9)^4=6561$, find $9^4$.\n(b) A number multiplied by itself gives $372$. What does the negative of that number multiplied by itself give? Explain.",
        "solution_text": "(a) $9^4=6561$. The four negative signs in $(-9)^4$ pair up, so removing them leaves the value unchanged.\n(b) $372$. Both factors change sign. The two sign changes cancel, so the product is unchanged."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "Which has the smaller value, $(-3)^3$ or $(-2)^5$? Show how you decide.",
        "solution_text": "$(-3)^3=(-3)\\times(-3)\\times(-3)=-27$.\n$(-2)^5=(-2)\\times(-2)\\times(-2)\\times(-2)\\times(-2)=-32$.\n$-32$ is smaller than $-27$, so $(-2)^5$ has the smaller value."
      }
    ],
